It's not so hard as you might think. If you're used to Linux documentation,
you will find this a breeze. First, make a DOS boot disk . You can do this
in Win98 with either the 'rescue disk' or on the command line 'format a:/s".
If you make a boot disk, there will be a bunch of extra crap on the disk.
Get rid of all of it. All you need is command.com. Alternatively, you can
use FreeDOS. I'm not familiar with it, but I bet that it's first thing is a
DOS boot floppy.

Then, create a ram disk. You'll need to add a file called config.sys to the
boot floppy. Also, put himem.sys on the disk Then, add a these lines in the
config.sys

 DEVICE=HIMEM.SYS
DEVICE=RAMDRIVE.SYS 1024 /E

Where 1024 is the size of the drive and E is the drive letter. Adapt as
necessary.

All you need next is the compressed NH exectuable, and an unzipping program
that will fit on the disk. You can unzip NH to the ramdrive and launch it
using an autoexec.bat file with these lines:

@echo off
unzip nethack.zip e:
e:/nethack.exe

The first line turns off screen echos.



